course: dictionary
lesson: 11348
title: Zigzag: lines and movement
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can be a different part of speech, and that changes how you use it. Zigzag can be a noun, an adjective, a verb or an adverb. «The lightning made a zigzag across the dark sky.» Here zigzag is a noun, a thing you can see: a line that goes sharply one way and then sharply the other way.
explain: «The path zigzags up the steep hill.» Zigzags is a verb, an action. The clues are steep hill and up: a path that goes straight up would be very hard to climb, so the path turns from side to side as it climbs. To zigzag means to move forward by turning from side to side, again and again.
explain: «Some spiders weave zigzag silk decorations into their webs.» Here zigzag comes before a noun, silk, and tells us what kind of silk it is. That makes zigzag an adjective. «A fox trots past the bins, then zigzags away» shows the same action: a rabbit that zigzags is hard to catch, because it keeps changing direction.
fact: A zigzag is a line that goes sharply one way, then sharply the other way, again and again, like the letter Z or W.
fact: «Zigzags» can be a verb: to zigzag means to move forward by turning from side to side, again and again.
fact: «Zigzag» can be an adjective, as in «a zigzag pattern», meaning shaped like a zigzag line.
fact: In the UK, zigzag lines painted on the road near crossings mean drivers must not park there.
fact: An adverb tells how something happens, as in «run zigzag»: the runner moves from side to side as they go.
exercise: «The adder has a dark zigzag down its back.» What is a zigzag? | *A line that goes sharply one way and then the other, again and again | A round spot | A straight line that goes up to the sky
exercise: «A huge furry bumblebee zigzags low over the lawn.» What does zigzags mean here? | Flies straight up into the sky | Sits still and buzzes | *Moves forward by turning from side to side, again and again | Falls onto the grass
exercise: «Some spiders weave zigzag silk decorations into their webs.» Which word is an adjective? | spiders | weave | *zigzag | webs
test: Which picture shows a zigzag line? | *A line like the letter W | A straight line | A circle | A single dot
test: «The path zigzags up the steep hill.» What does the path do as it climbs? | *Turns from side to side as it climbs | Runs down to the river | Disappears into the trees | Goes straight up
exam: «A fox trots past the bins, and a rabbit freezes, then zigzags away.» What does zigzags mean here? | Runs fast in a straight line | Stays very still | *Moves away by turning from side to side | Jumps over the bins
